From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:09:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: Read T8132 readiness on the J604
 as well

Shared PMP power commands (the G16 AGX vote, the DCP DISP vote) wait for
the PMP report of their supplier to show ready before they are sent. The
T8132 report is only recognised on the J713; on any other machine a
declared report must be the J613 25G83 one, so on the J604 every such
command fails with -ENODEV before anything reaches the PMP. The G16 probe
then stops with "PMP AGX vote failed: -19".

The J604 is the same T8132 SoC with the same PMP: its Apple device tree
maps the same report window (pmgr and mcc ranges at 0x3803c0000 + 0x20000)
as the J713's, and its PMP firmware is started the same way. Treat it
like the J713 here. The readiness check only reads the report status.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index 5d77d1761b..b650c55707 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -279,7 +279,8 @@ int apple_pmp_report_wait_supplier_ready(struct device *supplier, unsigned int t
 	struct platform_device *pdev;
 	struct apple_pmp_report *rep;
 	u64 status;
-	bool t8132 = of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") &&
+	bool t8132 = (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") ||
+		      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j604")) &&
 		of_device_is_compatible(supplier->of_node, "apple,t8132-pmp-v2");
 	int ret;
 
